Dante acquired an Ignatius Amulet while on an expedition to Chile. {{Source|Huntik.com|Webisodes}}

Dante brought Ignatius specially on a mission to [[Iceland]], where it was used to melt [[Ymir]]'s [[Ice Creature]] army. Dante later used it together with [[Lok]]'s [[Kipperin]] to make a ring of fire in the air in order to help form the [[Rainbow Bridge]] to [[Thor]]'s temple. {{source|The Legacy of Thor}}

While infiltrating [[Klaus' bookshop]], Dante called upon Ignatius again. This time, Ignatius was used to burn away a swarm of Mutant Flying Spiders created by [[Klaus]], while Dante and his team were protected by the spell [[Chillskin]]. {{source|The Bookshop Hunter}}

Ignatius was summoned yet again for a fight against [[the Professor]] due to being immune to [[Araknos|Araknos']] mind control. It, with the aid of Zhalia Moon, tried to keep Araknos under control; however, when Tao managed to overpower the Titans attacking it, it was able to send Ignatius back to its amulet. {{source|The Mission}}

Whilst exploring [[Cortés' Vault]] with [[Metagolem]], Dante invoked Ignatius to defend him from [[Hernán Cortés]]' traps. {{source|Gremlow Infestation!}}

Upon arriving at the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]], Dante summoned Ignatius to stop [[Tantras]] from gaining the power of the [[Heart of Vlad Dracul]]. By using [[Copykind]], Dante used Ignatius' burn ability to distract Tantras and defeat [[Antedeluvian|Powerbonded Antedeluvian]]. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}
